WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.390
This is Knoxville Flooring's application,
built by Catalyst Innovations.

2
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.590
We are using sample information to show
how room measurements become an

3
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:12.510
estimate. Start by choosing a room and
entering its length and width.

4
00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:16.650
The estimator calculates the floor area,
keeping the measurements and the

5
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:20.190
quantity together. Next, review the
assumptions around the work.

6
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:24.570
Waste allowance, material costs, and labor
all affect the estimate.

7
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.090
Preparation matters too. The application
includes options for work such as

8
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:33.370
tear-out and subfloor repair, so those
details can be considered alongside

9
00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:37.830
the flooring itself. As the inputs change,
review the updated summary.

10
00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:42.270
It brings the quantity, entered costs,
suggested price, and estimated margin

11
00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:46.210
into one view. These are sample
calculations, not a promise of profit.

12
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:50.110
Finally, the proposal handoff provides a
next step from the estimate.

13
00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:53.550
We are stopping before creating or sending
anything to a customer.

14
00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:57.230
Measurements, job details, and pricing
stay connected.

15
00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:01.430
Talk with Catalyst about building software
around the way your team estimates

16
00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:02.690
and manages work.

